Apple's first smart glasses could arrive in a rapidly expanding market, with worldwide AI glasses shipments increasing 263% year-over-year during the first half of 2026, according to <a href="https://counterpointresearch.com/en/insights/global-ai-glasses-shipments-surge-263-percent-yoy-with-display-less-ai-glasses">Counterpoint Research</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2021/01/Apple-Glasses-Blue-Feature.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-777637" /><br/>
The figures are particularly relevant for Apple because display-less products accounted for 96% of shipments. Apple's <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/05/31/apple-glasses-late-2027-report/">initial smart glasses</a> are likewise rumored to omit an augmented reality display, focusing instead on audio, cameras, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a>, and connectivity with the iPhone and Apple's wider ecosystem.<br/>
<br/>
<em>Bloomberg</em>'s <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/mark-gurman/">Mark Gurman</a> reports that the company is targeting a late 2027 release for the device. Apple could introduce the glasses <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/07/26/apple-smart-glasses-wwdc-2027-report/">at WWDC 2027</a> with an emphasis on privacy.<br/>
<br/>
Counterpoint said shipments of display-less AI glasses increased 258% from the first half of 2025 and 22% from the preceding six months. This category includes products such as the Ray-Ban <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-glasses/">Meta</a> glasses, which provide photography, audio, calling, and AI features without screens.<br/>
<br/>
&zwnj;Meta&zwnj; currently presents Apple with a formidable incumbent. The company accounted for approximately 94% of total AI glasses shipments, while its own volume grew 260% year over year and 22% sequentially. Its expansion has been supported by additional frame styles, wider retail distribution, and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/06/23/meta-launches-its-own-299-smart-glasses/">new glasses priced from &#36;299</a>.<br/>
<br/>
Display-equipped AI glasses represented only 4% of the market, although shipments in that segment increased 449% year-over-year. Apple's more advanced augmented-reality glasses are <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/06/03/kuo-vision-pro-successors-nixed/">not expected until 2029 at the earliest</a>.<br/>
<br/>
Counterpoint identified increasing semiconductor costs and public unease about wearable cameras as possible obstacles to continued growth. It nevertheless expects investment from Apple, &zwnj;Meta&zwnj;, Google, and Samsung to push the category toward more proactive glasses that use AI to understand their surroundings and provide assistance based on context.<div class="linkback">Tags: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/counterpoint/">Counterpoint</a>, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/meta/">Meta</a></div><br/>This article, &quot;<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/22/apple-smart-glasses-to-enter-growing-market/">Apple&#039;s Smart Glasses to Enter a Rapidly Growing Market</a>&quot; first appeared on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com">MacRumors.com</a><br/><br/><a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/apples-smart-glasses-to-enter-a-rapidly-growing-market.2490206/">Discuss this article</a> in our forums<br/><br/>